{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-15237-r4524034","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Potato Soup","sourcePageId":15237,"sourceRevision":"4524034","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-15T20:00:17Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Potato%20Soup&oldid=4524034","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:20:28.261Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Polish recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for soup","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using carrot","Category:Recipes using cow milk","Category:Recipes using dehydrated broth","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes using potato","Category:Recipes with images"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"f3258deb2df1d67a85b3bca94162c5ebeddd3ed94498e573e8514b6dccd951d0","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Potato recipes|servings=4–5 people|time=90 minutes|difficulty=2\n| image = [[File:Three bowls of potato soup.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Soup|Soup]]\n\n==Ingredients==\n*6 [[Cookbook:Potato|potatoes]], peeled and [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n*3 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n*1 large [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrots]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n*¼ cup [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]] or [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]]\n*3 cups water\n*2 cubes [[Cookbook:Bouillon Cube|chicken bouillon]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] ground [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]] to taste\n*3 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Flour|all-purpose flour]]\n*1 tbsp dried [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]]\n*¼ tsp dried [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Cook onion in butter until tender.\n#Bring the diced potatoes, carrots, water and chicken bouillon in another stock pot to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]]. [[Cookbook:Simmering|Simmer]] about 10 minutes or until tender. Add ground black pepper.\n#Add the flour to the cooked onions to make a paste. Stir in the milk. Cook over low heat stirring constantly until warmed through. Add the potato and carrot mixture. Stir in the parsley and thyme and heat through. Serve hot.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n*Use vegetable [[Cookbook:Stock|stock]] instead of chicken bouillon for a vegetarian soup.\n*Add [[Cookbook:Leek|leeks]] if available.\n*Omit all ingredients except potatoes, water, salt and pepper for a simple and surprisingly pleasing potato soup. High quality, flavorful potatoes are required for this variation, which itself presents an ideal base for an inventive cook to expand upon.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using potato]]\n[[Category:Polish recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for soup]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cow milk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dehydrated broth]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]\n\n[[sr:Кувар:Кромпир чорба]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Potato Soup","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"6 potatoes, peeled and diced","sourceText":"6 potatoes, peeled and diced","amountText":"6 potatoes, peeled and d